# PRE-COMMIT LENS COMPLIANCE CHECK

## Forbidden Imports — REJECT if found:
- `from 'styled-components'`
- `from '@emotion/react'` (direct app use — internal Lens use is fine)
- `from '@emotion/styled'` (direct app use — internal Lens use is fine)
- `from '@chakra-ui'`
- `from '@mui/'`
- `from 'antd'`
- `from 'react-bootstrap'`
- `from 'react-icons'`
- `from '@heroicons'`
- `from 'lucide-react'`
- `from '@headlessui'`
- `from '@radix-ui'`
- `*.module.css`
- `*.css'`
- `*.scss'`

## Forbidden JSX — REJECT if found:

### Interactive primitives (linter enforces these — always forbidden):
- `<button>` → use `<Button>`
- `<input>` → use `<TextInput>`, `<Checkbox>`, `<Radio>`, `<Switch>`
- `<select>` → use `<Select>`
- `<textarea>` → use `<Textarea>`
- `<a>` → use `<Link>`

### Styling violations (linter enforces these — always forbidden):
- `style={{` — inline styles, always forbidden, no exceptions
- `className=` with values not in `mastery-db.json` approvedClasses
- `className={` — dynamic className expressions, always forbidden

### Raw HTML layout elements — PREFER Lens, but wrappers are allowed:
```
<div>, <span> are ALLOWED as wrapper elements when:
  ✅ A Lens layout component (Split, Arrange, Container) cannot solve the need
  ✅ React interop is required (refs, portals, event boundaries)
  ✅ They are styled only with static Lens utility classes from mastery-db.json

<div>, <span> are FORBIDDEN when:
  ❌ They replace a Lens layout component (<Split>, <Arrange>, <Container>)
  ❌ They carry inline styles
  ❌ They carry className values not in mastery-db.json

<p>, <h1>-<h6>, <span> for semantic text:
  → Convention (not linter-enforced): use <Text htmlTag="p"> instead
  → These will not fail CI but violate the coding standard

<ul>, <ol>, <li> → use <List> / <ListRow>
<img> → use <Avatar>, <Logo>, or <Illustration>
<form> → use Lens form components wrapped in a <Container>
<table>, <thead>, <tbody>, <tr>, <td> → escalate as LENS-GAP if needed
<nav>, <header>, <footer>, <section>, <aside>, <main>, <article>
  → Use <Container htmlTag="nav"> etc. (htmlTag prop controls semantic element)
<hr> → use <Container borderSide="bottom" />
```

## Wrong Prop Names — CORRECT these:
- `disabled` → `isDisabled`
- `loading` → `hasLoader`
- `as="..."` → `htmlTag="..."`
- `leftIcon` → `iconBefore`
- `rightIcon` → `iconAfter`
- `size="sm"` → `size="small"`
- `size="md"` → `size="medium"`
- `size="lg"` → `size="large"`
- `variant="ghost"` → does not exist in Lens
- `ref={ref}` → `refHandler={(r) => { ref.current = r }}`
- `padding="4"` → `padding="medium"` or `padding={2}` (number × 8px)
- `gap="2"` → `gap="small"`

## Forbidden Files — NEVER create:
- Any `.css` file
- Any `.scss` file
- Any `.styled.ts` file
- `tailwind.config.*`